        "name": null,
        "sourceIndex": 0,
        "steps": [
          {
            "sourceIndex": 0,
            "text": "Rinse and drain berries, add sugar and puree until smooth.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4854"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 1,
            "text": "Pass the puree through a fine sieve, to remove all tiny seeds.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4855"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 2,
            "text": "You will need about 1/2 cup of puree for dipping the ladyfingers. The rest pour into the saucepan.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4856"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 3,
            "text": "Add 4-5 Tbsp of cold water to gelatin, and set it aside.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4857"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 4,
            "text": "Place the saucepan with berry mixture over medium heat on the stove (don't boil), remove from the stove and add gelatin. Whisk well until the gelatin is dissolved. Let it cool to room temperature. ...",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4858"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 5,
            "text": "Pour the very cold heavy whipping cream into a large bowl and whisk, until the cream reaches the soft peaks stage. Do not over beat!",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4859"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 6,
            "text": "Once the berry puree is completely at room temperature, gently fold it into the whipped cream and set it aside.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4860"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 7,
            "text": "Line the inside and walls of a springform pan with parchment paper or plastic wrap. ...",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4861"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 8,
            "text": "Measure the length you need.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4870"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 9,
            "text": "You can trim off one end of each ladyfinger.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4862"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 10,
            "text": "Dip one side of the ladyfinger in the puree mixture. Let the excess syrup drip off, then line the ladyfingers (dipped side needs to be inside) in a tight ring, cut side down, around the spring form pan.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4864"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 11,
            "text": "If you having trouble fitting the last ladyfinger in, you can cut it in half.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4871"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 12,
            "text": "Pour the berry mousse into the springform. Cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate for at least 6 hours.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4865"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 13,
            "text": "Carefully remove springform walls and plastic wrap. Transfer cake to the plate.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4866"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 14,
            "text": "Dust with cocoa powder.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4867"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 15,
            "text": "Garnish with some fresh berries, fresh mint, whipped cream and shredded chocolate.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4851"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 16,
            "text": "You can decorate with ribbon, but don't forget to remove the ribbon before cutting the cake. :)",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:4868"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
